                         1950 | ;   ALLOCATION MAP
                         1951 | ;
                         1952 | ;   ENTRY PARAMETERS:(BC)   CURRENT BLOCK NUMBER OR 0000H
                         1953 | ;               (SEE NOTE BELOW)
                         1954 | ;   EXIT PARAMETERS: (HL)   NUMBER OF NEXT FREE BLOCK OR
                         1955 | ;               0000H IF NO BLOCK AVAILABLE
                         1956 | ;
                         1957 | ;   NOTE:
                         1958 | ;       SEARCH STARTS AT BLOCK 0000H FOR FIRST ALLOC-
                         1959 | ;       ATION FOR A NEW DIRECTORY EXTENT, OR FROM THE
                         1960 | ;       CURRENT BLOCK NUMBER FOR SUBSEQUENT ALLOCATIONS
                         1961 | ;       THIS SAVES TIME SINCE IT ASSUMES THAT ALL
                         1962 | ;       BLOCKS UP TO THE CURRENT ONE HAVE BEEN USED.
                         1963 | ;       THIS MAY CAUSE AN 'OUT OF DISK SPACE' ERROR
                         1964 | ;       IF OTHER FILES ARE BEING DELETED WHILE THIS
                         1965 | ;       ONE IS BEING WRITTEN. A REMOTE, BUT REAL,
                         1966 | ;       POSSIBILITY.
                         1967 | ;
